          </div>
          <div class="ev-assump-control">
            <div class="seg-control seg-2" role="group" aria-label="Price assumption">
              <button type="button" class="ev-basis-btn seg-btn is-active" data-basis="trend"><span class="ev-basis-text">Reverts to trend</span><span class="help-tip" tabindex="0">?<span class="tip-content">The primary projection. Values your stack at the Power Law <em>trend</em> price throughout, including today. Withdrawals are taken against this trend-priced stack to fund retirement income. This is the central-case expectation if you assume bitcoin mean-reverts to trend over your retirement window.</span></span></button>
              <button type="button" class="ev-basis-btn seg-btn" data-basis="current"><span class="ev-basis-text">Today&rsquo;s gap to trend persists</span><span class="help-tip" tabindex="0">?<span class="tip-content">Anchors to today&rsquo;s actual market price and projects forward at the same Power Law growth rate. When this basis sits <em>below</em> the trend basis, bitcoin is below trend today &mdash; the gap is the extra gain if the market mean-reverts to trend over your retirement window. When <em>above</em>, the gap is a premium that trend says will fade. Useful as a sanity check: to assume <em>no</em> mean-reversion, plan closer to this basis.</span></span></button>
            </div>
          </div>

          <div class="ev-assump-label">Show values in
            <span class="help-tip" tabindex="0">?<span class="tip-content">A display basis only &mdash; it changes how figures are labeled and deflated, never the projection itself.</span></span>
          </div>
          <div class="ev-assump-control">
            <div class="seg-control seg-2" role="group" aria-label="Dollar basis">
              <button type="button" class="ev-dollars-btn seg-btn is-active" data-dollars="real">Real (today&rsquo;s $ &middot; <span class="seg-btn-sub">&mdash;</span>)<span class="help-tip" tabindex="0">?<span class="tip-content">Today&rsquo;s purchasing power &mdash; every figure divided back by your chosen inflation rate (set under &ldquo;Assumptions &mdash; change&rdquo;, below the year-by-year strip), so amounts are comparable to money now.</span></span></button>
              <button type="button" class="ev-dollars-btn seg-btn" data-dollars="nominal">Nominal (future $)<span class="help-tip" tabindex="0">?<span class="tip-content">Raw future dollars &mdash; the actual dollar amounts in each year, inflation included. price &times; BTC = value reconciles exactly in this mode.</span></span></button>
            </div>
          </div>

          <div class="ev-assump-label">Interpret my retirement income as
            <span class="help-tip" tabindex="0">?<span class="tip-content">A behavioral setting on the withdrawal itself, independent of the display basis above. You can be in the real-dollar view with a same-every-year plan.</span></span>
          </div>
          <div class="ev-assump-control">
            <div class="seg-control seg-2" role="group" aria-label="Income basis">
              <button type="button" class="seg-btn is-active" data-incbasis="today">Rises with inflation<span class="help-tip" tabindex="0">?<span class="tip-content">Your <strong>retirement income</strong> target is in today&rsquo;s purchasing power. Each retirement year draws the same real amount &mdash; so the <em>nominal</em> (future-dollar) figure rises with inflation to preserve what it buys. Standard for retirement planning.</span></span></button>
              <button type="button" class="seg-btn" data-incbasis="fixed">Same every year<span class="help-tip" tabindex="0">?<span class="tip-content">Your <strong>retirement income</strong> target is a fixed nominal amount &mdash; the same raw dollars every year. Because prices rise, its <em>real</em> (today&rsquo;s-dollars) purchasing power shrinks over time.</span></span></button>
            </div>
          </div>

          <div class="ev-assump-label">Years in retirement
            <span class="help-tip" tabindex="0">?<span class="tip-content">The modeled horizon. &ldquo;Permanently exceeds spending&rdquo; is checked across this whole span, not asserted from a single crossing &mdash; so a longer horizon is a harder test, because the Power Law&rsquo;s trend growth rate declines with time.</span></span>
          </div>
          <div class="ev-assump-control">
            <div class="seg-control" role="group" aria-label="Years in retirement" data-grad="years">
              <button type="button" class="seg-btn" data-years="20">20</button>
              <button type="button" class="seg-btn is-active" data-years="30">30</button>
              <button type="button" class="seg-btn" data-years="40">40</button>
            </div>
          </div>

          <div class="ev-assump-label">Inflation rate
            <span class="help-tip" tabindex="0">?<span class="tip-content">Saved on this device and shared across every calculator on the site. Changing it here changes it everywhere.</span></span>
          </div>
          <div class="ev-assump-control">
            <div class="seg-control" role="group" aria-label="Inflation rate" data-dim="inflation">
              <button type="button" class="seg-btn" data-preset="cpi-official">3.5% <span class="seg-btn-sub">CPI</span></button>
              <button type="button" class="seg-btn" data-preset="m2-growth">6.5% <span class="seg-btn-sub">M2</span></button>
              <button type="button" class="seg-btn" data-preset="shadow-stats">8% <span class="seg-btn-sub">Shadow</span></button>
            </div>
            <p class="ev-assump-inherited" data-inherited="inflation" hidden></p>
          </div>

          <div class="ev-assump-label">Bitcoin growth model
            <span class="help-tip" tabindex="0">?<span class="tip-content">Saved on this device and shared across every calculator on the site. <a href="/the-power-law.html#summary">What is the Power Law?</a></span></span>
          </div>
          <div class="ev-assump-control">
            <div class="seg-control" role="group" aria-label="Bitcoin growth model" data-dim="btcGrowthModel">
              <button type="button" class="seg-btn" data-preset="powerlaw-floor">Floor band</button>
              <button type="button" class="seg-btn" data-preset="powerlaw-trend">Trend line</button>
            </div>
            <p class="ev-assump-inherited" data-inherited="btcGrowthModel" hidden></p>
          </div>

        </div>
        <p class="ev-assump-foot">Inflation and growth model are saved on this device only and shared with every other calculator on the site. Everything else on this card is page-local. Defaults are starting positions, never recommendations.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

